<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka lists 3 firms in telecom privatisation.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka lists 3 firms in telecom privatisation.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three foreign telephone firms have been shortlisted for the second round of bidding for part privatisation of the state-owned Sri Lanka Telecom, finance ministry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said Japan's NTT, France Telecom and Korea Telecom have been shortlsted for the second round of bids to identify a strategic investor in Sri Lanka Telecom.</p>
<p>Six potential investors had put in their bids to buy 35 percent of Telecom's shares and take over the management, they said.</p>
</text>
